 ('1897030',
  'Efficient Windows logging for Incident Response : A comparison of logging '
  'strategies for malware and threat detection (Effektiv loggning för '
  'Incidenthantering i Windows : En jämförelse av loggingsstrategier för '
  'detektion av skadlig programvara och hot)',
  '\n'
  'as cyberattacks are becoming increasingly common, so are incidents. '
  'incident responders use information from logs to perform mitigation and '
  'recovery, and to prepare for future incidents. many organisations do not '
  'employ measured logging strategies and are consequently only equipped with '
  'default configurations, such as the default windows logging configuration, '
  'that produce logs which are insufficient for incident response. the aim of '
  'this thesis is to determine the capabilities of common windows logging '
  'strategies when it comes to detecting threats and providing information in '
  'the case of an incident investigation. in this study, a comparison was made '
  'between three windows logging configurations: standard windows log '
  'configuration, advanced audit policy for windows and the system monitor '
  '(sysmon) service for windows. the three configurations were all exposed to '
  'the same series of threats and were scored based both on their ability to '
  'generate relevant logs for each threat and on the amount of relevant '
  'information included in the logs. the results showed that, unsurprisingly, '
  'the standard windows log configuration is far from sufficient in both its '
  'detection capabilities and in the relevance of the information it provides. '
  'it was also confirmed that no single configuration is sufficient to detect '
  'all of the threats included in the study. it is therefore recommended to '
  'both utilize advanced audit policies and the sysmon service when auditing '
  'real systems.\n'
  '\n'),
 ('811172',
  'The Efficiency of Double-Decked Elevators : A comparison between '
