  '\n'
  'between predator and prey. we hoped to find signs of\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'mimicry as well, but classic mimicry was not found in the\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'results.\n'
  '\n'),
 ('668818',
  'Crowding through narrow spaces',
  '\n'
  'this report compares two steering behavior algorithms in\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'crowded path following. both steering and path following\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'could be a part of a flocking simulation. the report is\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'divided into two parts, one introductory part which explains\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'what a flocking simulation is, what the goal of the report is\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'and what methodology is used to acquire that goal. the\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'introductory part is followed by the concepts part. in the\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'concepts part there will be an extensive explanation of the\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'path following algorithm used as it’s a core function. a\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'solid understanding will aid the conviction that excluding\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'certain common behaviors are legitimate for the purpose of\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'comparing the two steering algorithms. there’s also\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'sections for other behaviors such as steering and separation.\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'in conclusion either of the steering algorithms\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  '1 could be\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'used in a very crowded path traversal simulation.\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'this report was made independently and without\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'collaboration.\n'
  '\n'),
 ('700130',
  'Path Planning for Autonomous Heavy DutyVehicles in Unknown Environments '
  'using GraphSearch',
  '\n'
  'the vision of autonomous vehicles is becoming a reality. advanced driver '
  'assistance systems have the potential to improve transportation safety and '
  'efficiency, and offer the possibility of environmental and economical '
  'gains. however, navigation and control of autonomous vehicles is an '
  'intricate task. the vehicle needs to make decisions and respond to '
  'situations on its own.\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'graph-search based route planning has the potential to reduce replanning '
  'times and provides the end-user with feasible and optimized plans. this '
  'thesis adopts the real-time capable, re-planning <em>d</em><em>lite '
  '</em>algorithm as a powerful planning workhorse. the algorithm conducts '
  'graph-search on a state lattice graph, and uses motion primitives to '
  'construct a plan. the route planner inherently handles inexact motion, '
  'which lends itself well in practice as the vehicle cannot be expected to '
  'follow instructions to the letter.\n'
  '\n'
  '\n'
  'the route planner is able to plan in large and obstacle-laden cavelike '
  'terrains, and according to a cost map (e.g. a map pointing out '
  'fuelefficient routes), with an average re-planning time of less than '
  '0<em>.</em>1 seconds. the state lattice graph is by construction feasible, '
  'which renders the planned path of the route planner physically possible for '
  'the vehicle to follow in practice.\n'
  '\n'),
 ('703048',
  'Human following behavior for an autonomousmobile robot (Människoföljande '
  'beteenden för autonoma mobilarobotar)',
  '\n'
  "robots are used more and more to change people's life. in recent times, "
  'some robots have found their place in houses. those robots are specic ones '
  "as for example robotic vacuum cleaners. the next step in robotics' "
  'evolution is to make people live with robots in everyday life. this project '
  'attempts to make a robot follow a person. to achieve that, a people '
  'detector using a rgb-d sensor is implemented. the result of this detector '
  'is sent to a tracking algorithm using depth segmentation and a region '
  'growing algorithm. at the end, a navigation algorithm containing path '
  'planning and obstacle avoidance is used to make the mobile robot move. this '
  'method can make the robot follow a person that walks slowly in front of it. '
  'suggestions are presented to improve the method and adapt it to everyday '
  'life. thanks to this study, mobile robots can be used in personal home and '
  'assist people. an application could be for example to follow a person that '
  'needs medical assistance and help this person when necessary.\n'
  '\n'),
 ('700130',
